w":92,"column":27,"value":"A gate in a City Wall that allows water (such as a river, Aqueduct, or Waterway) to enter the settlement. A Watergate has underwater defenses to block unwanted access. If you construct a Watergate when you construct a City Wall, the Watergate does not count toward the limit of the number of buildings you can construct per turn"},{"row":93,"column":1,"value":"Waterway"},{"row":93,"column":2,"value":"3"},{"row":93,"column":3,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":4,"value":"2"},{"row":93,"column":5,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":6,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":7,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":8,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":93,"column":9,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":93,"column":10,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":93,"column":11,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":12,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":93,"column":13,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":14,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":15,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":16,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":17,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":18,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":19,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":20,"value":"0"},{"row":93,"column":25,"value":"Counts as water district border for adjacent buildings"},{"row":93,"column":27,"value":"A river or canal occuping part of the District Grid. At the GM’s option, a natural Waterway may already exist on the grid, requiring no action or BP to build. If you construct a City Wall that touches or crosses the Waterway, you must also build Watergates on the same turn"},{"row":94,"column":1,"value":"Windmill"},{"row":94,"column":2,"value":"6"},{"row":94,"column":3,"value":"10"},{"row":94,"column":4,"value":"1"},{"row":94,"column":5,"value":"1"},{"row":94,"column":6,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":7,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":8,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":94,"column":9,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":94,"column":10,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":94,"column":11,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":12,"value":"Err:509"},{"row":94,"column":13,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":14,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":15,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":16,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":17,"value":"1"},{"row":94,"column":18,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":19,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":20,"value":"0"},{"row":94,"column":25,"value":"A Windmill adjacent to a Cistern or Granary increases the Stability bonus provided by that building by +1"}]},{"name":"Terrain_Improvements","nonemptyRows":13,"maxRow":14,"maxColumn":5,"formulaCount":0,"inputCount":63,"functions":{},"dependencies":{},"formulas":[],"inputs":[{"row":2,"column":1,"value":"Jody Cummings:Improvements in RED can share the same hex as other improvements.Name"},{"row":2,"column":2,"value":"Terrain"},{"row":2,"column":3,"value":"Effect"},{"row":2,"column":4,"value":"Cost"},{"row":2,"column":5,"value":"Description"},{"row":3,"column":1,"value":"Aqueduct*"},{"row":3,"column":2,"value":"One end must be hill or mountain hex; can pass through any type of hex"},{"row":3,"column":3,"value":"Loyalty+1, Stability +1, allows settlement to build water-dependent buildings"},{"row":3,"column":4,"value":"As a Road, except the cost is not doubled for hexes with rivers (See Table 4–6: Terrain Imp. On page 214)"},{"row":3,"column":5,"value":"An Aqueduct brings water from alpine lakes and rivers to lowland cities where water is scarce or insufficient for the local populace. A finished series of Aqueduct hexes must connect to a hill or mountain hex (with a river or lake) on one end and a settlement on the other end; otherwise, youdo not gain its benefit."},{"row":4,"column":1,"value":"Bridge*"},{"row":4,"column":4,"value":"When you build a Road in a hex that contains a river, the doubled coast of the Road includes the cost of bridges needed to cross the river. You don’t need to build a Bridge as a separate unit; it’s listed here for reference only"},{"row":4,"column":5,"value":"A Bridge allows your Road hexes to cross rivers"},{"row":5,"column":1,"value":"Canal*"},{"row":5,"column":2,"value":"Desert, hill, or plain"},{"row":5,"column":3,"value":"Settlements in a hex with a Canal treat the hex as if it had a river"},{"row":5,"column":4,"value":"(See Table 4–6: Terrain Imp. On page 214)"},{"row":5,"column":5,"value":"A Canal is an artificial waterway that allows barge traffic to haul heavy commodities"},{"row":6,"column":1,"value":"Farm*"},{"row":6,"column":2,"value":"Desert (requires canal, coastline, or river), hill, or plain"},{"row":6,"column":3,"value":"Consumption decreases by 2 BP"},{"row":6,"column":4,"value":"(See Table 4–6: Terrain Imp. On page 214)"},{"row":6,"column":5,"value":"A Farm helps feed your kingdom"},{"row":7,"column":1,"value":"Fishery*"},{"row":7,"column":2,"value":"Coastline, water, river, or marsh"},{"row":7,"column":3,"value":"Consumption decreases by 1 BP"},{"row":7,"column":4,"value":"4 BP"},{"row":7,"column":5,"value":"A Fishery is like a Farm, except it provides abundant fish rather than planted crops"},{"row":8,"column":1,"value":"Fort*"},{"row":8,"column":2,"value":"Any land"},{"row":8,"column":3,"value":"Stability +2, Defense +4, increase Consumption by 1 BP;Unrest decreases by 1 when completed.If this hex becomes a settlement, this improvement counts as one Barracks and one Stables building"},{"row":8,"column":4,"value":"24 BP"},{"row":8,"column":5,"value":"A Fort is a walled encampment for military forces outside a settlement. You can upgrade a Watchtower to a Fort (Unrest decreases when you do so, just as if you had built the Fort from scratch)"},{"row":9,"column":1,"value":"Highway*"},{"row":9,"column":2,"value":"Any hex with a Road"},{"row":9,"column":3,"value":"Economy +1 for every 4 hexes of Highway, Stability +1 for every 8 hexes of Highway;Improves overland travel speed (Pathfinder RPG Core Rulebook 172"},{"row":9,"column":4,"value":"Twice the cost of a Road (See Table 4–6: Terrain Imp. On page 214)"},{"row":9,"column":5,"value":"A highway is a paved and well-maintained version of a Road. You may upgradea Road into a Highway. Kingdom Size must be 26 or greater to build a Highway"},{"row":10,"column":1,"value":"Mine"},{"row":10,"column":2,"value":"Cavern, desert, hill, or mountain"},{"row":10,"column":3,"value":"Economy +1, earn +1 BP per turn when collecting taxes during the Income phase"},{"row":10,"column":4,"value":"6 BP"},{"row":10,"column":5,"value":"A Mine extracts metal, coal, salt, or other useful materials from the earth"},{"row":11,"column":1,"value":"Quarry"},{"row":11,"column":2,"value":"Cavern, hill, or mountain"},{"row":11,"column":3,"value":"Stability +1, earn +1 BP per turn when collecting taxes during the Income phase"},{"row":11,"column":4,"value":"6 BP"},{"row":11,"column":5,"value":"A Quarry extracts workable stone from the ground"},{"row":12,"column":1,"value":"Road*"},{"row":12,"column":2,"value":"Any land"},{"row":12,"column":3,"value":"Economy +1 for every 4 hexes of Road, Stability +1 for every 8 hexes of Road;improves overland travel speed (Core Rulebook 172)"},{"row":12,"column":4,"value":"See the Road column of Table 4–6: Terrain Imp. On page 214"},{"row":12,"column":5,"value":"A Road speeds travel through your kingdom and promotes trade. You can upgrade a Road to a Highway"},{"row":13,"column":1,"value":"Sawmill"},{"row":13,"column":2,"value":"Forest or jungle"},{"row":13,"column":3,"value":"Stability +1, earn +1 BP per turn when collecting taxes during the Income phase"},{"row":13,"column":4,"value":"3 BP"},{"row":13,"column":5,"value":"A sawmill centralizes the activities of loggers and turns trees into lumber for use in building and crafting"},{"row":14,"column":1,"value":"Watchtower*"},{"row":14,"column":2,"value":"Any land"},{"row":14,"column":3,"value":"Stability +1, Defense +2; Unrest decreases by 1 when completed.If this hex becomes a settlement, this improvement counts as a Watchtower"},{"row":14,"column":4,"value":"12 BP"},{"row":14,"column":5,"value":"A Watchtower flies your f lag, is a safe place for your patrols, and establishes your power on the frontier. A Watchtower cannot